    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, null, null, 3, 5]\np = 2, q = 8  ->  6\np = 2, q = 4  ->  2    (a node is its own ancestor)\np = 3, q = 5  ->  4\np = 7, q = 9  ->  8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In a general binary tree you'd have to search both subtrees. In a BST the values tell you where p and q are. If **both** are smaller than the current node, both live in the left subtree — so does their LCA. If both are bigger, go right. The first node where they **split** (one on each side, or one of them is the node) is the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Ignore the order: general binary-tree LCA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The classic binary-tree solution works on a BST too: ask each subtree whether it contains p or q, and the node where both sides answer \"yes\" is the LCA."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function lowestCommonAncestor(root, p, q) {\n  if (root === null || root === p || root === q) return root;\n  const left = lowestCommonAncestor(root.left, p, q);\n  const right = lowestCommonAncestor(root.right, p, q);\n  if (left !== null && right !== null) return root;   // one on each side\n  return left !== null ? left : right;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    if root is None or root is p or root is q:\n        return root\n    left = lowest_common_ancestor(root.left, p, q)\n    right = lowest_common_ancestor(root.right, p, q)\n    if left is not None and right is not None:\n        return root                       # one on each side\n    return left if left is not None else right"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {\n    if (root == null || root == p || root == q) return root;\n    TreeNode left = lowestCommonAncestor(root.left, p, q);\n    TreeNode right = lowestCommonAncestor(root.right, p, q);\n    if (left != null && right != null) return root;      // one on each side\n    return left != null ? left : right;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {\n    if (root == nullptr || root == p || root == q) return root;\n    TreeNode* left = lowestCommonAncestor(root->left, p, q);\n    TreeNode* right = lowestCommonAncestor(root->right, p, q);\n    if (left != nullptr && right != nullptr) return root;   // one on each side\n    return left != nullptr ? left : right;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** It may visit every node — it never uses the ordering."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Recursion that follows the values"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function lowestCommonAncestor(root, p, q) {\n  if (p.val < root.val && q.val < root.val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root.left, p, q);\n  if (p.val > root.val && q.val > root.val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root.right, p, q);\n  return root;                                         // they split here (or one of them is root)\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    if p.val < root.val and q.val < root.val:\n        return lowest_common_ancestor(root.left, p, q)\n    if p.val > root.val and q.val > root.val:\n        return lowest_common_ancestor(root.right, p, q)\n    return root                           # they split here (or one of them is root)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {\n    if (p.val < root.val && q.val < root.val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root.left, p, q);\n    if (p.val > root.val && q.val > root.val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root.right, p, q);\n    return root;                                         // they split here (or one of them is root)\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {\n    if (p->val < root->val && q->val < root->val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root->left, p, q);\n    if (p->val > root->val && q->val > root->val) return lowestCommonAncestor(root->right, p, q);\n    return root;                                         // they split here (or one of them is root)\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h), space O(h)** for the call stack — one call per level on a single path."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. The same walk as a loop"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "lca-bst",
      "caption": "Both smaller: go left. Both bigger: go right. Otherwise this node is where they split."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function lowestCommonAncestor(root, p, q) {\n  let node = root;\n  while (node !== null) {\n    if (p.val < node.val && q.val < node.val) node = node.left;        // both on the left\n    else if (p.val > node.val && q.val > node.val) node = node.right;  // both on the right\n    else return node;                                                   // they split here\n  }\n  return null;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    node = root\n    while node is not None:\n        if p.val < node.val and q.val < node.val:\n            node = node.left              # both on the left\n        elif p.val > node.val and q.val > node.val:\n            node = node.right             # both on the right\n        else:\n            return node                   # they split here\n    return None"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {\n    TreeNode node = root;\n    while (node != null) {\n        if (p.val < node.val && q.val < node.val) node = node.left;         // both on the left\n        else if (p.val > node.val && q.val > node.val) node = node.right;   // both on the right\n        else return node;                                                    // they split here\n    }\n    return null;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {\n    TreeNode* node = root;\n    while (node != nullptr) {\n        if (p->val < node->val && q->val < node->val) node = node->left;         // both on the left\n        else if (p->val > node->val && q->val > node->val) node = node->right;   // both on the right\n        else return node;                                                         // they split here\n    }\n    return nullptr;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h), space O(1).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Ignore the order: general binary-tree LCA",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "It may visit **every node**, never using the ordering.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The call stack is as deep as the **height**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Recursion that follows the values",
          "time": "O(h)",
          "timeWhy": "Each call goes **one way** until p and q split: a single path.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "One call per level on that path."
        },
        {
          "approach": "The same walk as a loop",
          "time": "O(h)",
          "timeWhy": "The **same single path** down.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "Only the **current node**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**p is an ancestor of q** — the answer is p itself.",
        "**p = q** — the answer is that node.",
        "**p and q on opposite sides of the root** — the root.",
        "**A skewed tree** — h = n, so O(h) becomes O(n)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**LCA of a binary tree** — no ordering to follow; approach 1 is the answer there.",
        "**Distance between two nodes in a BST** — depth(p) + depth(q) − 2·depth(LCA).",
        "**LCA where p or q may be missing** — search for both first, then run the walk."
      ]
    }
  ],
